Task 4 is done. `pnpm test` passes (302 tests) and `pnpm typecheck` is clean. I did not commit or touch `.kiro/agents`.

- **Tool:** `scan_links` is in `packages/lychgate-mcp/src/tools.ts` and registered in `server.ts`. It takes exactly one of `path`, `markdown`, `url` or `repo`, plus an optional `citeDate`. It runs the same `runScan` engine as `/api/scan`.
- **Output:** the first text block is a summary with the health score, class counts and any cap notes, followed by up to 20 non-living links. The second block is JSON with the full summary and all non-living results. Living links are left out of the results. Results are sorted worst first, using the `ORDER` list the web app already uses.
- **Caps:** the 300-link cap is reported when hit, and the 120 s budget is passed to `runScan` (the 300-link cap is `runScan`'s existing limit). If time runs out, the unfinished links come back as restless and the text says so.
- **Tests:** I added six tests to `tests/mcp-tools.test.ts`, written before the code. They cover ordering, both caps, the exactly-one-input rule, `url` and `repo` inputs, and `path`.
- **Tick and log:** the task is ticked in `tasks.md`, and `KIRO_USAGE.md` has the dated line crediting the `gravedigger` agent via `scripts/kiro/run-task.sh mcp-server 4`.

**Early path check:** `path` needed a working-directory check, because otherwise it would read arbitrary files. I added a basic one that rejects `..`, absolute paths outside the working directory and symlink escapes. Task 5 is still open for the fast-check property test.

I also had to make the hung-transport test mock honour `init.signal`. Otherwise it never aborted and the test timed out.
